  "authoringNote": "SPEC R04 requires the order to follow completion of the encounter. The final order (2026-09-02) is dated eight days before the final encounter (2026-09-10), so the pair holds R04.order_before_encounter, a conflict for the administrative reviewer; this is the before-encounter chronology case of row F05 (outside the interval that starts at the encounter), isolated from F14x2 where the same key appears among several conditions. order_after_bound does not hold (the order is not after 2027-03-10) and the identifiers match. R04 cites status, date and practitioner identifier of both documents (six) and names no parent (C07). R05 compares the receipt only with the order it references (C06): 2026-09-03T17:05:00Z is after the order date span 2026-09-01T10:00Z to 2026-09-03T12:00Z, so R05 passes; the receipt preceding the encounter is not an R05 matter. R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review.",
